DYNARR - grow a buffer with realloc and return the sum of 1..n.

Language features
  - the C dynamic-memory API in a seed: realloc (grow one element at a time)
  - aligned_alloc for a cache-aligned scratch copy
  - malloc/free draw from the seed heap

Try it
  SEED h%, "DYNARR.SED"
    PRINT CALL(h%, 100)          -> 5050

Build it on the machine
  grow dynarr          # -> build/DYNARR.SED
  (grow links the berry-libc from SEEDCORE.PKT for this one automatically)
It is also prebuilt in /SEED as DYNARR.SED, ready to use.

